# Client Component Naming Convention

React components that include `"use client"` at the top must use the `*.client.tsx` file naming convention.

## Rule

- Any `.tsx` file that starts with `"use client"` must be named `ComponentName.client.tsx`
- Server components and shared utilities retain their default naming (e.g. `Header.tsx`, `Footer.tsx`)
- This keeps server/client boundaries explicit and visible at the file-system level

## Examples

**Correct:**
- `Header.client.tsx` — contains `"use client"`, interactive header with scroll animations
- `MenuOverlay.client.tsx` — contains `"use client"`, animated overlay component
- `DarkModeToggle.tsx` — UI primitive that happens to be a client component (exception for small isolated UI primitives in `components/ui/`)

**Incorrect:**
- `HeaderClient.tsx` — suffix style is wrong; use `Header.client.tsx` instead
- `Header.tsx` — if this file contains `"use client"`, it must be renamed to `Header.client.tsx`

## Rationale

The `*.client.tsx` suffix mirrors Next.js conventions and makes the server/client split immediately visible when browsing the file tree, without needing to open each file.
